Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] FEXCore: slice1 #DE for div/idiv

Every change is guarded by fexc_slice1; the code is in
tools/fexc/shim/fexc_sites.inc and fexc_precision.h.

Dispatcher: DIVOp/IDIVOp record the x86 operand width of each div/idiv
(fexc_div_width, keyed by the guest RIP); FEX's IR widens the 8-bit forms.

JIT: Arm64JITCore::FexcBeforeOp emits, before each UDiv/Div op, a
flag-free zero-divisor and quotient-overflow check on the op's operand
registers that branches to a `brk #3` divide stub (FexcDivCheck). After
the call to the LUDIV/LDIV helper of a 64-bit divide with a 128-bit
dividend, FexcDivAfterCall branches to a divide stub when the helper
reports #DE in x2.

Flag elimination: a divide op is a fault point like a guest memory
access (FexcPrecision::FaultPoint): it reads all six flags, keeps the
incoming flags live at its instruction start, and gets the pre-NZCV
save after an NZCV writer of its instruction.
